---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/maitreya.jpg';
---

<Base title="About — Maitreya Sapariya" description="Background, current role, and what I'm working toward.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero about-head">
      <div class="about-head-text">
        <p class="kicker reveal">about</p>
        <h1 class="reveal">Engineer first, still figuring the rest out in public.</h1>
      </div>
      <Image
        class="portrait reveal"
        src={portrait}
        alt="Maitreya Sapariya standing outdoors in a black blazer and glasses, smiling"
        width={352}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        loading="eager"
      />
    </section>

    <section class="section prose">
      <p>
        I finished a B.E. in Artificial Intelligence and Data Science at A. D. Patel
        Institute of Technology, CVM University, in Anand, Gujarat, in 2026. I'm now
        a Software Engineer at Crest Infosystems, having converted from intern to
        full-time after a six-month internship.
      </p>

      <p>
        The work I care most about sits where machine learning meets production
        software: not a notebook that proves a model can work, but a system that
        keeps working once real people depend on it. <a href="/projects">Maatritwa
        AI</a>, a maternal-health risk system for rural India, is where I've put
        that belief into practice so far.
      </p>

      <h2>Finland, briefly</h2>
      <p>
        In August 2025 I attended the 34th Jyväskylä Summer School in Finland, on
        machine learning and stochastic control, and used the trip to solo-travel
        through Finland, Sweden, Norway, Latvia, and Estonia. It's the trip that
        made the idea of an Erasmus Mundus programme feel concrete instead of
        aspirational. In 2026 I followed up with JYU's COG1 course, attended
        virtually around a full-time work schedule, and submitted the written
        project report that came with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Where I'm headed</h2>
      <p>
        I'm building toward the EDISS Erasmus Mundus Joint Master's programme,
        Engineering of Data-Intensive Intelligent Software Systems, for a
        September 2027 start. Not because a scholarship page told me to want it,
        but because the programme's own framing, bridging data science and
        software engineering rather than treating them as separate disciplines,
        matches how I already think about the work. The <a href="/log">log</a> is
        the honest version of how that's going.
      </p>

      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AWS Certified AI Practitioner</li>
        <li>AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer – Associate</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
